# Socket exclusions — https://docs.socket.dev/docs/socketignore
#
# The same single exclusion as `socket.yml`'s `projectIgnorePaths`, repeated
# here because the two formats are read by different paths and it was not
# known which one the skills.sh upload pipeline uses.
#
# Evidence for adding it, and honest status of the claim it makes:
#
#   * 30 Sep 2026, 12:10 UTC — a fresh re-audit pinned the current commit
#     (pkg purl `31da9fee…`, v1.5.0) and dropped the first of the two alerts
#     outright, but still reported `tests/fixtures/audits/security.mjs`.
#     `socket.yml` had carried this exclusion since `819fc6e`, so the
#     pipeline evidently does not consult `socket.yml`.
#   * A second install run minutes later did not re-audit at all —
#     `auditedAt` stayed at `2026-09-30T12:10:48.409Z`. So **this file is
#     untested**: it is the other documented format for the same request, not
#     a verified fix.
#
# Re-check: when `auditedAt` advances past 12:10 UTC on 30 Sep 2026, read
# https://skills.sh/ahaomar/un-editorial-check/un-editorial-check/security/socket.
# If the fixture alert is gone, this format is the one the pipeline reads and
# the note should say so plainly. If it is still there, neither format is
# honoured and the remaining moves are upstream: a Socket false-positive
# review, or an issue on vercel-labs/skills. Do not restructure the fixture to
# satisfy a scanner — it is never executed, and its literal sinks are the
# subject of the test.
#
# Patterns work like .gitignore patterns; Socket's defaults (.git,
# node_modules, coverage and the rest) apply alongside them.
#
# `tests/fixtures/audits/security.mjs` is a deliberate test fixture that is
# never executed. It contains literal `el.innerHTML = …` and `eval(code)` so
# the suite can prove that a scanner reading it flags them. A scanner reading
# it as source reports the fixture's own contents as though this repository
# had written them — which is the alert this file exists to remove.
tests/fixtures/audits/security.mjs
